Schema disclosure: Workflow tool_input shape is SCHEMA-DOC-DERIVED (R5), not captured live -- the bare single-argument call form (agent(prompt), no opts object) is documented in the Workflow tool's own agent( ) API as the plain shorthand call shape, not observed from a live session.

Pins the reviewer's recall gap: a call with no opts object -- agent("run the nightly sweep") -- can never carry a model: key (there is no object literal to put one in), so this shape is unpinned BY DEFINITION and the guard must deny it. Under a scanner that only opens/closes blocks on the literal substring "})", a bare call like this never produces a "})" of its own (its only closing token is a bare ")"), so a line-buffered scanner keeps accumulating lines until the NEXT call's "})" closes the (now merged) block -- and if that next call happens to be pinned, the merged block reads as pinned too, silently allowing the bare call. This fixture pairs the bare unpinned call with a second, separately and correctly pinned object-style call on the next line specifically to catch that merge-and-launder failure mode. Expected result: deny, naming the offending call via the fragment "run the nightly sweep" (extracted from the bare string argument itself, since there is no prompt: key to match).
